  "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-6)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 4 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$Ax=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
